{"id":"cartridges-anatomy","rev":1,"lang":"en","status":"published","review_flag":null,"disclaimer":null,"title":"Anatomy of a cartridge","summary":"Hull, primer, powder, wad, shot and crimp: what is inside a clay cartridge, how each part affects the shot and which cartridges the rules of Sporting™ and Compak® Sporting ban.","body":[{"k":"gear-cartridges-p1","t":"p","html":"A <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/cartridge/\">cartridge</a> holds everything for one shot: the <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/hull/\">hull</a> with a metal head, the <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/primer/\">primer</a>, <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/powder/\">powder</a>, the <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/wad/\">wad</a> and the shot. Shooters also say shell. 'Empties' are fired hulls.","disc":null,"rule_ref":null,"anchor":"gear-cartridges"},{"k":"dg-cartridge-cutaway","t":"diagram","html":"<figure class=\"dg\" aria-labelledby=\"dg-cartridge-cutaway\"><p class=\"dg-h\" id=\"dg-cartridge-cutaway\">A cartridge cut lengthwise</p><svg class=\"dg-svg\" viewBox=\"40 70 520 250\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"dg-cartridge-cutaway\" focusable=\"false\"><rect class=\"dg-c1\" x=\"96\" y=\"96\" width=\"440\" height=\"138\" rx=\"3\"/><rect class=\"dg-cut\" x=\"104\" y=\"104\" width=\"424\" height=\"122\"/>\n<path class=\"dg-c2\" d=\"M58 86h20v6h80v146h-80v6h-20z\"/><rect class=\"dg-c3\" x=\"58\" y=\"148\" width=\"26\" height=\"34\" rx=\"2\"/>\n<rect class=\"dg-c4\" x=\"158\" y=\"104\" width=\"54\" height=\"122\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"164\" cy=\"114\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"171.5\" cy=\"122\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"179\" cy=\"114\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"186.5\" cy=\"122\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"194\" cy=\"114\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"201.5\" cy=\"122\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"209\" cy=\"114\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"164\" cy=\"150\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"171.5\" cy=\"142\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"179\" cy=\"150\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"186.5\" cy=\"142\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"194\" cy=\"150\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"201.5\" cy=\"142\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"209\" cy=\"150\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"164\" cy=\"170\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"171.5\" cy=\"178\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"179\" cy=\"170\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"186.5\" cy=\"178\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"194\" cy=\"170\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"201.5\" cy=\"178\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"209\" cy=\"170\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"164\" cy=\"206\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"171.5\" cy=\"198\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"179\" cy=\"206\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"186.5\" cy=\"198\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"194\" cy=\"206\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"201.5\" cy=\"198\" r=\"1.8\"/><circle class=\"dg-gr\" cx=\"209\" cy=\"206\" r=\"1.8\"/>\n<rect class=\"dg-c5\" x=\"212\" y=\"104\" width=\"16\" height=\"122\"/><path class=\"dg-c5l\" d=\"M228 112 l11 106 l11 -106 l11 106 l11 -106M272 106h194M272 224h194M272 106v118\"/>\n<circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"282\" cy=\"116\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"293.8\" cy=\"116\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"305.6\" cy=\"116\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"317.4\" cy=\"116\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"329.2\" cy=\"116\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"341\" cy=\"116\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"352.8\" cy=\"116\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"364.6\" cy=\"116\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"376.4\" cy=\"116\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"388.2\" cy=\"116\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"400\" cy=\"116\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"411.8\" cy=\"116\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"423.6\" cy=\"116\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"435.4\" cy=\"116\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"447.20000000000005\" cy=\"116\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"459\" cy=\"116\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"287\" cy=\"135.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"298.8\" cy=\"135.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"310.6\" cy=\"135.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"322.4\" cy=\"135.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"334.2\" cy=\"135.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"346\" cy=\"135.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"357.8\" cy=\"135.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"369.6\" cy=\"135.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"381.4\" cy=\"135.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"393.2\" cy=\"135.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"405\" cy=\"135.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"416.8\" cy=\"135.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"428.6\" cy=\"135.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"440.4\" cy=\"135.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"452.20000000000005\" cy=\"135.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"464\" cy=\"135.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"282\" cy=\"155\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"293.8\" cy=\"155\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"305.6\" cy=\"155\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"317.4\" cy=\"155\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"329.2\" cy=\"155\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"341\" cy=\"155\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"352.8\" cy=\"155\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"364.6\" cy=\"155\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"376.4\" cy=\"155\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"388.2\" cy=\"155\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"400\" cy=\"155\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"411.8\" cy=\"155\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"423.6\" cy=\"155\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"435.4\" cy=\"155\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"447.20000000000005\" cy=\"155\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"459\" cy=\"155\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"287\" cy=\"174.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"298.8\" cy=\"174.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"310.6\" cy=\"174.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"322.4\" cy=\"174.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"334.2\" cy=\"174.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"346\" cy=\"174.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"357.8\" cy=\"174.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"369.6\" cy=\"174.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"381.4\" cy=\"174.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"393.2\" cy=\"174.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"405\" cy=\"174.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"416.8\" cy=\"174.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"428.6\" cy=\"174.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"440.4\" cy=\"174.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"452.20000000000005\" cy=\"174.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"464\" cy=\"174.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"282\" cy=\"194\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"293.8\" cy=\"194\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"305.6\" cy=\"194\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"317.4\" cy=\"194\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"329.2\" cy=\"194\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"341\" cy=\"194\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"352.8\" cy=\"194\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"364.6\" cy=\"194\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"376.4\" cy=\"194\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"388.2\" cy=\"194\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"400\" cy=\"194\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"411.8\" cy=\"194\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"423.6\" cy=\"194\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"435.4\" cy=\"194\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"447.20000000000005\" cy=\"194\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"459\" cy=\"194\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"287\" cy=\"213.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"298.8\" cy=\"213.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"310.6\" cy=\"213.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"322.4\" cy=\"213.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"334.2\" cy=\"213.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"346\" cy=\"213.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"357.8\" cy=\"213.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"369.6\" cy=\"213.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"381.4\" cy=\"213.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"393.2\" cy=\"213.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"405\" cy=\"213.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"416.8\" cy=\"213.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"428.6\" cy=\"213.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"440.4\" cy=\"213.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"452.20000000000005\" cy=\"213.5\" r=\"5\"/><circle class=\"dg-c6\" cx=\"464\" cy=\"213.5\" r=\"5\"/>\n<path class=\"dg-c7\" d=\"M468 104 L530 165 L468 226 M498 104 L530 165 L498 226 M528 104 L530 165 L528 226\"/>\n<g class=\"dg-dm\"><path d=\"M58 272v18M536 272v18M58 282h478\"/><text x=\"297\" y=\"306\" text-anchor=\"middle\">fired hull: usually 65–70 mm</text></g><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"360\" cy=\"98\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"360\" y=\"98\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">1</text></g><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"92\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">2</text></g><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"71\" cy=\"165\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"71\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">3</text></g><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"185\" cy=\"120\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"185\" y=\"120\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">4</text></g><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"245\" cy=\"216\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"245\" y=\"216\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">5</text></g><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"400\" cy=\"150\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"400\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">6</text></g><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"515\" cy=\"165\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"515\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">7</text></g></svg><ol class=\"dg-leg\"><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">1</b>Hull (plastic or paper)</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">2</b>Metal head</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">3</b>Primer</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">4</b>Powder</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">5</b>Wad</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">6</b>Shot</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">7</b>Crimp (a star of 6 or 8 folds)</li></ol><figcaption>What is inside one cartridge, from the metal head to the crimp.</figcaption></figure>","disc":null,"rule_ref":null},{"k":"cartridges-anatomy-p2","t":"p","html":"The hull, or case, is a tube, most often plastic, with a metal head at the bottom. Paper hulls exist too, and some grounds prefer them because they leave less litter. A fired hull is usually 65–70 mm long, and it must suit the <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/chamber/\">chamber</a> of your gun (see <a href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/learn/gun-gauge-and-barrels/\">Gauge and barrel length</a>).","disc":null,"rule_ref":null},{"k":"cartridges-anatomy-p3","t":"p","html":"In the centre of the head sits the primer. When the firing pin strikes it, the primer gives a spark and ignites the powder. The powder does not explode but burns very fast, and the gases push the shot charge up the barrel.","disc":null,"rule_ref":null},{"k":"cartridges-anatomy-p4","t":"p","html":"Between the powder and the shot sits the wad. It works like a plug: it stops the hot gas blowing past the pellets, cushions the push and keeps the pellets together as they travel up the barrel. A plastic wad usually has a cup that protects the pellets and often gives a slightly tighter pattern.","disc":null,"rule_ref":null},{"k":"cartridges-anatomy-p8","t":"p","html":"A <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/fibre-wad/\">fibre or felt wad</a> breaks down in nature, so many grounds insist on it. Biodegradable plastic wads also exist, but some grounds do not accept them.","disc":null,"rule_ref":null},{"k":"cartridges-anatomy-p5","t":"p","html":"Above the wad is the shot: several hundred small pellets. The top of the hull is closed by the <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/crimp/\">crimp</a>, most often a star of 6 or 8 folds. A good crimp holds everything firmly in place and helps each cartridge fire the same way as the last.","disc":null,"rule_ref":null},{"k":"cartridges-anatomy-p6","t":"p","html":"The FITASC rules of Parcours de Chasse – Sporting™ and Compak® Sporting ban reloaded cartridges, that is, fired hulls filled again, for example at home. They also ban dispersers (inserts that spread the shot wider on purpose) and any other special device inside the cartridge. Mixed shot of different sizes or qualities, black powder and tracers (cartridges that leave a glowing trail) are banned too. So for competitions bring factory cartridges that comply with the rules.","disc":"both","rule_ref":null},{"k":"cartridges-anatomy-p7","t":"tip","html":"The box usually shows the gauge, hull length, load, shot number or diameter, shot material and wad type, and often the velocity. Learn to read the box, and you will know what you are loading.","disc":null,"rule_ref":null},{"k":"gear-cartridges-p5","t":"p","html":"Some grounds add their own environmental rules for practice, for example fibre wads only or steel shot only: check the ground's rules before a trip. Empty cases go into the bin on the stand, and shooters with semi-automatics pick up their ejected cases when they leave.","disc":"both","rule_ref":null},{"k":"cartridges-anatomy-p9","t":"p","html":"Three numbers on the box have lessons of their own: the gauge (<a href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/learn/gun-gauge-and-barrels/\">Gauge and barrel length</a>), the shot size (<a href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/learn/cartridges-shot-size/\">Shot size</a>) and the load (<a href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/learn/cartridges-load-weight/\">Load weight</a>).","disc":null,"rule_ref":null}],"notes":[],"phrases":[{"k":"gear-cartridges-ph3","speaker":"coach","en":"Empties in the bin, please, not on the grass.","meaning":"Put fired hulls into the container.","say":null,"audio":1},{"k":"gear-cartridges-ph4","speaker":"coach","en":"Steel only on this ground.","meaning":"Lead shot is not allowed on this ground (a local rule, not a FITASC one).","say":null,"audio":1}],"key_points":[{"k":"gear-cartridges-kp1","html":"Cartridge = hull, primer, powder, wad, shot.","checklist":false},{"k":"cartridges-anatomy-kp2","html":"Plastic wad: often a slightly tighter pattern; fibre wad: breaks down in nature.","checklist":false},{"k":"cartridges-anatomy-kp4","html":"FITASC bans reloads, dispersers, mixed shot, black powder and tracers.","checklist":false},{"k":"cartridges-anatomy-kp5","html":"Read the box: gauge, length, load, shot, wad.","checklist":false},{"k":"gear-cartridges-kp5","html":"Empties go in the bin; semi-auto users pick up their cases.","checklist":false}],"did_you_know":{"k":"cartridges-anatomy-dyk","html":"After the shot a plastic wad flies on for several tens of metres beyond the stand. That is why the fields around old grounds can be full of wads, whereas fibre gradually breaks down."},"quiz":[{"k":"cartridges-anatomy-q1","q":"What ignites the powder in a cartridge?","options":[{"k":"a","text":"The wad"},{"k":"b","text":"The primer"},{"k":"c","text":"The crimp"},{"k":"d","text":"The shot"}],"correct":"b","explain":"The firing pin strikes the primer, which ignites the powder."},{"k":"cartridges-anatomy-q2","q":"Why do many grounds require fibre wads?","options":[{"k":"a","text":"They are cheaper"},{"k":"b","text":"They give a tighter pattern"},{"k":"c","text":"They break down in nature"},{"k":"d","text":"FITASC requires it"}],"correct":"c","explain":"Fibre and felt break down, while ordinary plastic wads stay in the fields for years."},{"k":"cartridges-anatomy-q3","q":"Which cartridges do the FITASC rules ban?","options":[{"k":"a","text":"Factory loads with a plastic wad"},{"k":"b","text":"Factory loads with a fibre wad"},{"k":"c","text":"Paper-hulled cartridges"},{"k":"d","text":"Reloaded cartridges"}],"correct":"d","explain":"Reloaded cartridges, dispersers, mixed shot, black powder and tracers are banned.","rule_ref":"sporting:ch7-cartridges","disc":"both"}],"terms":[{"id":"cartridge","en":"Cartridge","local":"","label":"Cartridge","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/cartridge/"},{"id":"hull","en":"Hull","local":"","label":"Hull","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/hull/"},{"id":"primer","en":"Primer","local":"","label":"Primer","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/primer/"},{"id":"powder","en":"Powder","local":"","label":"Powder","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/powder/"},{"id":"wad","en":"Wad","local":"","label":"Wad","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/wad/"},{"id":"fibre-wad","en":"Fibre wad","local":"","label":"Fibre wad","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/fibre-wad/"},{"id":"crimp","en":"Crimp","local":"","label":"Crimp","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/crimp/"},{"id":"chamber","en":"Chamber","local":"","label":"Chamber","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/chamber/"},{"id":"empties","en":"Empty cases","local":"","label":"Empty cases","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/empties/"},{"id":"semi-automatic","en":"Semi-automatic","local":"","label":"Semi-automatic","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/semi-automatic/"},{"id":"steel-shot","en":"Steel shot","local":"","label":"Steel shot","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/steel-shot/"},{"id":"shot-size","en":"Shot size","local":"","label":"Shot size","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/shot-size/"},{"id":"load-weight","en":"Load weight","local":"","label":"Load weight","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/load-weight/"},{"id":"gauge","en":"Gauge","local":"","label":"Gauge","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/gauge/"}],"rule_refs":[{"book":"sporting","id":"ch7-cartridges","label":"Chapter 7 · Cartridge rules","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/rules/en/sporting/weapons-and-ammunition/#ch7-cartridges"},{"book":"compak","id":"ch18-cartridge-bans","label":"Chapter 18 · Prohibited ammunition","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/rules/en/compak/shooting-equipment/#ch18-cartridge-bans"},{"book":"sporting","id":"ch8-turning-empties","label":"Chapter 8 · Turning around; empty cases","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/rules/en/sporting/rules-of-conduct-safety/#ch8-turning-empties"},{"book":"compak","id":"ch18-empty-cases","label":"Chapter 18 · Disposing of empty cases","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/rules/en/compak/shooting-equipment/#ch18-empty-cases"}],"sources":[{"title":"FITASC — official rules of Parcours de Chasse – Sporting™ and Compak® Sporting","url":"https://www.fitasc.com/disciplines-sportives/reglements-sportifs","fitasc":true},{"title":"C.I.P. — tables of dimensions of cartridges and chambers (TDCC), including shot cartridges","url":"https://www.cip-bobp.org/en/tdcc","fitasc":false}],"evidence":[],"more_in_en":0}
